The whole point of the tournament is that people can compare results 
directly, under the same circumstances. If there are 100 different 
seeds, there might as well not be seeds at all, because no one will 
remember the different games they played.

On the other hand, if a player is allowed to play the same seed twice, 
he can use the effect to emulate savescumming. The first time he plays, 
he records his keystrokes. The second time he plays, he plays back all 
but the last 100 turns from his previous game, and continues from 
there. Duplicate NetHack ensures that two players making the same moves 
will end up at the same place, so blindly playing back moves WILL work. 
And allowing that is clearly a Bad Thing.

